" and Object Environments, within the tools provided by EaaSI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:24
msgid "What resources *should* be published?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:27
msgid ""
"Once published to the network, removing or deleting an environment may "
"have severe technical repercussions, since users at other nodes may have "
"generated derivatives from that environment, which would break."
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:30
msgid ""
"Nodes and users are advised to use the beta testing period to consider "
"how to design and enforce local workflows for publishing resources, given"
" these technical restrictions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:33
msgid ""
"When selecting Base and Software Environments to share with the rest of "
"the network, EaaSI users and admins can consider questions posed by the "
"`Code of Best Practices in Fair Use for Software Preservation "
"<https://www.arl.org/storage/documents/publications/2018.09.24_softwarepreservationcode.pdf>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:36
msgid ""
"Did you lawfully acquire your copy of the software included in the "
"environment?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:37
msgid "Is the software still reasonably available in the commercial marketplace?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:38
msgid ""
"Are there any limitations present in donation or acquisition agreements "
"that might preclude fair use?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:39
msgid "What license(s) was the software distributed under?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:41
msgid ""
"The resources and environments provided by Yale University Library will "
"hopefully provide illustrative examples for the type of content that "
"might be appropriate to share, but this will also be an ongoing, "
"collaborative conversation within the network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:48
msgid "How to publish Base and Software Environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:50
msgid ""
"To publish a Base Environment from your local node to the network, locate"
" the selected environment in the *Private* sub-section of the \"Base "
"Environment\" tab of the Environments overview page. In the \"Actions\" "
"dropdown menu, select \"Details\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../legacy/publishing.rst:56
msgid ""
"In the top right corner of the environment detail page, click the "
"\"Publish\" button:"
msgstr ""

